.TH "CSSROTATE.CSSROTATE" "3JS" "August 11, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
CSSRotate.CSSRotate \- CSSRotate: CSSRotate() constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]CSSRotate()\f[B]\f[R] constructor creates a new
\f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] object representing the \f[CR]rotate()\f[R] value
of the individual \f[CR]transform\f[R] property in CSS.
.PP
This can be specified as either a 2D rotation by a particular angle, or
as a 3D rotation by an angle around a particular axis.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new CSSRotate(angle)
new CSSRotate(x, y, z, angle)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]angle\f[R]
A value for the angle of the \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] object to be
constructed.
This must be a \f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]x\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A value for the x\-axis of the \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] object to be
constructed.
This must either be a number (which is wrapped into a
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] of \f[CR]unit: \(dqnumber\(dq\f[R]) or a
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
Only used, and required, when constructing a 3D rotation.
.TP
\f[B]y\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A value for the y\-axis of the \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] object to be
constructed.
This must either be a number (which is wrapped into a
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] of \f[CR]unit: \(dqnumber\(dq\f[R]) or a
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
Only used, and required, when constructing a 3D rotation.
.TP
\f[B]z\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
A value for the z\-axis of the \f[CR]CSSRotate\f[R] object to be
constructed.
This must either be a number (which is wrapped into a
\f[CR]CSSUnitValue\f[R] of \f[CR]unit: \(dqnumber\(dq\f[R]) or a
\f[CR]CSSNumericValue\f[R].
Only used, and required, when constructing a 3D rotation.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]TypeError\f[R]
Raised if the value of \f[CR]CSSRotate.angle\f[R] is not an <angle>
value or \f[CR]CSSRotate.x\f[R], \f[CR]CSSRotate.y\f[R],
\f[CR]CSSRotate.z\f[R] are not <number> values.
.SH EXAMPLES
